<title>SINGAPORE: F&amp;N 1996 net profit up 18.2 pct.</title>
<headline>F&amp;N 1996 net profit up 18.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months ending September 30 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		    218.43  vs  184.76</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	 74.80  vs   64.80</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)     11.00  vs   10.00</p>
<p>    Turnover (billion)	    2.81  vs    2.53</p>
<p>    Investment income	     7.01  vs    6.90</p>
<p>    Other income		   35.03  vs   16.53</p>
<p>    Interest expense	     33.87  vs   27.82</p>
<p>    Operating pretax	    420.29  vs  361.51</p>
<p>    Associates		     29.67  vs   33.45</p>
<p>    Tax			     145.63  vs  130.53</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (85.90) vs  (79.67)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	     194.94  vs   46.41</p>
<p>    Div register/pay - March 10 1997/ March 21 1997  </p>
<p>Note- Food and beverage group Fraser &amp; Neave Ltd said the extraordinary gains were due to profit of S$178.38 million from sale of shares arising from the restructuring of its Malaysian operations and S$106.26 million revaluation surplus from land realised based on percentage of completion of properties under development minus fixed assets write off of S$8.19 million and provision for dimunition in value of other investments of S$81.51 million.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
